## Context

The `## Bibliography` section of `slides/manuscript/main.md` is a `[PLACEHOLDER]`. The document uses `[@key]` pandoc-citeproc citations throughout, resolving against `report/refs.bib`. The current pandoc invocation in `slides/Makefile` (or equivalent) omits `--citeproc`, so all cite keys render verbatim in the output PDF.

The Bibliography placeholder also documents the manual pandoc command:
`pandoc slides/manuscript/main.md -o slides/manuscript/main.pdf --pdf-engine=tectonic --resource-path=slides --citeproc --bibliography=report/refs.bib`

A Makefile target needs to encode this permanently.

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.md` — the manuscript with cite keys
- `report/refs.bib` — the BibTeX bibliography
- `slides/Makefile` or equivalent build file — needs the new target

## Actions

1. Locate the current Makefile that builds `slides/manuscript/main.pdf`.
2. Add or update the target to pass `--citeproc --bibliography=report/refs.bib` to pandoc.
3. Replace the `## Bibliography` `[PLACEHOLDER]` note with a brief note pointing to `report/refs.bib` (since citeproc auto-populates the section).
4. Verify the built PDF renders all citations and the bibliography section.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make slides/manuscript/main.pdf` (or equivalent) builds without error and with citations rendered
- [ ] The `## Bibliography` section is no longer a placeholder
- [ ] `make check` passes
